<name>SRS Airbag &amp; Seat Belt</name>
<section id="1000Y_S0012" variety="S0012">
<name>SRS Airbag</name>
<ttl id="1000Y_S0012_745Q2_T00B8" variety="T00B8">
<name>SRS Airbag System</name>
<para id="RM000000ELG00KX" category="C" type-id="305DK" name-id="554H0-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B1803</dtccode>
<dtcname>Driver airbag ignition circuit (short to +B)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000ELG00KX_05" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00006C200000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The driver side squib circuit consists of the airbag computer assembly, spiral cable and horn button assembly. When the activation conditions are met, the horn button assembly (driver airbag) is activated.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When a short to B+ is detected in the driver side squib circuit (D+, D- lines), DTC B1803 is stored in the airbag computer assembly.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="01" colname="C01" colwidth="0.97948     in"/>
<colspec colnum="02" colname="C02" colwidth="2.9949     in"/>
<colspec colnum="03" colname="C03" colwidth="3.172547     in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Trouble Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B1803</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" align="left">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Short to B+ in D+, D- lines of the wire harness between the airbag computer assembly and horn button assembly (driver side airbag)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Horn button assembly (driver side airbag) malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Spiral cable malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag Computer Assembly Malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" align="left">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Instrument panel wire (between airbag computer assembly and spiral cable)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Horn Button Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Spiral Cable</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag Computer Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000ELG00KX_06" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00006C300000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C159577J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000ELG00KX_07" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00006C400000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>When performing the simulation method, use TaSCAN to select check mode first. (see <xref href="RM00000050J01GX" label="Seep01"/>)</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000ELG00KX_08" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0013" proc-id="RM0550J___00006C500000">
<testtitle>Connector Inspection</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the battery negative terminal and wait for 90 seconds.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Make sure the ignition switch is OFF before disconnecting the cable from the negative (-) battery terminal.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the connection condition of the connectors connected to the airbag computer assembly, horn button assembly and spiral cable.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>The connector is connected properly</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the connectors connected to the airbag computer assembly, horn button assembly and spiral cable, and check the condition of the terminals of each connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>The terminals are not deformed or damaged</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the condition of the short pins of the connectors with a short mechanism on the instrument panel wire and spiral cable.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>The short pins are not deformed or damaged</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0014" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0026" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0014" proc-id="RM0550J___00006C600000">
<testtitle>Inspect Driver Side Airbag Squib Circuit (Airbag Computer Assembly - Horn Button Assembly)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref href="RM0000005D701ZX" label="Seep01"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect connectors C and D.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146169J04" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the cable to the negative (-) battery terminal and turn the ignition switch ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between each terminal of connector E and body ground.</ptxt>
<table>
<title>Voltage:</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.19in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.98in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2 (D+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1V or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1 (D-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1V or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0015" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0020" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0015" proc-id="RM0550J___00006C700000">
<scantool type="2"/>
<testtitle>Clear DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn IG OFF.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146174J02" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the battery negative terminal and wait for 90 seconds.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the connector to the airbag computer assembly.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using a wire harness (wire diameter 0.5mm), connect the terminals of connector E.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>When connecting the terminals, do not forcibly insert the wire harness into the connector terminals.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the battery negative terminal, turn IG ON and wait for 60 seconds.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), clear the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000050J01GX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0016" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0016" proc-id="RM0550J___00006C800000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Inspect Airbag Computer Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), check the DTCs. (see <xref href="RM00000050J01GX" label="Seep01"/>)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.06in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.07in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<ptxt>DTC B1803 is not output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<ptxt>DTC B1803 is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0017" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0022" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0017" proc-id="RM0550J___00006C900000">
<scantool type="2"/>
<testtitle>Clear DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn IG OFF.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146171J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the battery negative terminal and wait for 90 seconds.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the wire between the terminals of connector E, and connect the connector to the horn button assembly.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the battery negative terminal, turn IG ON and wait for 60 seconds.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), clear the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000050J01GX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000ELG00KX_08_0018" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
